From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:59:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: soc: samsung: exynos-sysreg: add gs201 HSI1

The HSI1 system registers of Google's gs201 hold the PCIe GEN4A_0
shareability (I/O coherency) control. There is no CMU_HSI1 driver yet, so
it is listed without a required bus clock.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/samsung,exynos-sysreg.yaml   | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/samsung,exynos-sysreg.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/samsung,exynos-sysreg.yaml
index 8cb6ce85d..6c33a6194 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/samsung,exynos-sysreg.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/samsung/samsung,exynos-sysreg.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ properties:
               - google,gs101-peric1-sysreg
               - google,gs201-apm-sysreg
               - google,gs201-csis-sysreg
+              - google,gs201-hsi1-sysreg
               - google,gs201-hsi2-sysreg
               - google,gs201-peric0-sysreg
               - google,gs201-peric1-sysreg
